# API contract

`contracts/openapi.yaml` is the composed public contract. Do not edit it by
hand for module endpoints: edit the matching fragment under
`contracts/modules/` and run `make contracts`.

- `contracts/base/openapi.yaml` — base document, security scheme and shared
  metadata.
- `contracts/modules/*.yaml` — one fragment per selected module.
- `contracts/compose.py` — deterministic merge; `--check` fails when the
  composed output is stale.
- `contracts/events.json` — streaming event union used by the agent run
  endpoint and the UI.

Generated clients:

- `apps/web/src/contracts/schema.d.ts` — TypeScript types from
  `openapi-typescript`; regenerate with `make contracts`.
- `contracts/generated/python/models.py` — Pydantic models from
  `datamodel-code-generator`; regenerate with `make contracts`.

Both are checked for staleness by `make contracts-check`. Swift, Kotlin and
Rust clients remain later; the native apps use hand-written DTOs against the
same shapes.

## Versioning and deprecation

- Public paths live under `/api/v1/`; `compose.py` rejects other prefixes.
- Within a version, changes are additive: new optional fields, endpoints and
  event types. Existing field names, types and status codes do not change.
- Breaking changes ship as a new version (`/api/v2/`) and run in parallel
  through a documented deprecation window. The old version is removed only
  after consumers have migrated.
- A deprecated endpoint or field is marked `deprecated: true` in the fragment
  and named in release notes with its replacement and removal target.
- Event types are append-only. Clients must ignore unknown event types and
  unknown fields; an existing type is never repurposed.
- Generated clients are updated in the same change as the contract, and
  `make contracts-check` plus `make contract-test` must pass.
